Q. 1. Create a STUDENT table using range or hash partitioning based on
the student marks or department. Perform DML operations such as
INSERT, UPDATE and DELETE on the partitioned table. Retrieve and
display records from each partition separately using suitable SQL
queries. Explain the working of partition-wise data storage.

ANS :-
-- Step 1: Create Database
CREATE DATABASE studentdb;

-- Step 2: Select Database
USE studentdb;

-- Step 3: Create Partitioned STUDENT Table
CREATE TABLE STUDENT (
    student_id INT NOT NULL,
    name VARCHAR(50),
    marks INT NOT NULL,
    PRIMARY KEY (student_id, marks)
)
PARTITION BY RANGE (marks) (
    PARTITION P0 VALUES LESS THAN (40),
    PARTITION P1 VALUES LESS THAN (60),
    PARTITION P2 VALUES LESS THAN (80),
    PARTITION P3 VALUES LESS THAN (101)
);

